<h2></h2>
<h2>Pull-offs</h2>
<p>Pull-offs are the exact opposite of hammer-ons. To play a pull-off, you =
play a note then you fret a note behind the one you just played, finally yo=
u pull your finger off the first note without re-plucking the string. Like =
hammer-ons, the notes will transition smoothly.</p>
<h3>Executing a Pull-off</h3>
<ol>
<li>Fret the first note.</li>
<li>Pluck the string.</li>
<li>Without releasing the first note, fret the second note with another fin=
ger.</li>
<li>While keeping the second note fretted, quickly release the first note.&=
nbsp; Do not pluck the string again.</li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
