<h3></h3>
<h3>Pre-bending</h3>
<p>Pre-bending is performed by bending the note before plucking the&nbsp;st=
ring so the pitch of the bent note is sounded.&nbsp; This is usually&nbsp;f=
ollowed by a release (explained below)</p>
<ol>
<li>Fret the note.</li>
<li>Push or pull the string vertically.</li>
<li>Pluck the string.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Release</h3>
<p>Releases almost always follow a pre-bent note.&nbsp; Often, they follow&=
nbsp;regular bent notes as well.&nbsp; Releasing is the act of returning to=
 the&nbsp;unbent note without letting go of the string.&nbsp; It=E2=80=99s =
done by reversing&nbsp;the bending process so you start with a bent note an=
d end with a normal&nbsp;fretted note.</p>
<ol>
<li>Bend or pre-bend a note.</li>
<li>Pluck the string.</li>
<li>While continuing to fret the note, return the string to an unbent posit=
ion.</li>
</ol>
